{{Quote|Either something is wrong with my photoreceptors&hellip;or a ship is touching down over there.|[[Teetee]]|<ref name="Misfit Droids">{{IDWAdventuresCite-2017|issue=15|story=Flight of the Falcon, Part 2: The Planet of Misfit Droids}}</ref>}}
'''Photoreceptors''', also known as '''visual sensors''', was a technical name for the optical sensors of a [[droid]]. They were the equivalent to an [[eye]].<ref name="databank" /> Numbers of photoreceptors could vary depending on the size and model of a droid. For instance, [[R2-D2]] had one, while [[EV-9D9]] had three. Many droids, like [[C-3PO]], had two.<ref name="Return of the Jedi">{{Film|VI}}</ref> Some could have them in different areas. For instance, [[General]] [[Grievous]]' [[IG-100 MagnaGuard|MagnaGuards]] had a built-in photoreceptor in their torso to allow them to fight without their heads.<ref name="Helmet Collection 24">{{HelmetCollectionCite|24|Helmets}}</ref>

